> Start with source scores whose losses can be checked by hand

For separate real and fake pools, this experiment uses a=0,b=c=1:

\[L_D=\tfrac12(\operatorname{mean}(r-1)^2+\operatorname{mean}f^2),\quad L_G=\tfrac12\operatorname{mean}(f-1)^2.\]

The half multiplies the sum of the two means, preserving the source Float32 grouping.
Derivatives are(r-1)/N,f/M for D, and(f-1)/M for G. For real scores(0,1,2) and
fake scores(-2,-1,0,1), D=13/12 and G=7/4. A confident wrong score keeps a nonzero
quadratic derivative. Scores remain unbounded. The cited paper also analyses different
labels a=-1,b=1,c=0 for its Pearson-divergence relation; that relation is not asserted
for this experiment's 0/1 targets. The explicit .5 reporting threshold below is a source
accuracy convention, not a fitted decision boundary or calibrated probability.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lsgan_derivatives.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::vector<double> x, dr, df, gf;
  for (int k = -60; k <= 60; ++k) {
    x.push_back(k / 20.);
    auto r          = n::full({1, 1}, k / 20., n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_(),
         f          = n::full({1, 1}, k / 20., n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
    const auto loss = n::models::LeastSquaresGanObjectives(r, f);
    const auto d    = n::grad(loss.discriminator, {r, f});
    dr.push_back(d[0].item());
    df.push_back(d[1].item());
    gf.push_back(n::grad(n::models::LeastSquaresGanObjectives(r, f).generator, {f})[0].item());
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(x, dr, "D real derivative", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .lines(x, df, "D fake derivative", {22, 163, 74}, 2.)
      .lines(x, gf, "G fake derivative", {220, 38, 38}, 2.)
      .y_limits(-4.5, 6)
      .x_label("Respective scalar raw source score")
      .y_label("Derivative; each pool size1")
      .title("LeastSquares objective: distinguish D and G directions")
      .save_svg("build/lsgan_derivatives.svg");
  auto r          = n::zeros({1, 1}, n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_(),
       f          = n::zeros({1, 1}, n::DType::Float64).requires_grad_();
  const auto loss = n::models::LeastSquaresGanObjectives(r, f);
  const auto d    = n::grad(loss.discriminator, {r, f});
  const auto g    = n::grad(n::models::LeastSquaresGanObjectives(r, f).generator, {f});
  std::print(
      "Hand-check: D={:.9f},G={:.9f}; D derivatives={},{}; G derivative={}.\n",
      loss.discriminator.item(),
      loss.generator.item(),
      d[0].item(),
      d[1].item(),
      g[0].item());
}
