> The held-out samples remain weak

| Fixed final diagnostic | Value |
|---|---:|
| D objective |0.0371180773|
| G objective |0.4426527023|
| Coarse-pixel MMD² |0.1181927919|
| Repeated fitting-mean MMD² |0.0001357794|
| D real/fake source accuracy |0.970/1.000|
| Generated mean pixel |0.4995838039|
| Mean per-pixel variance across generated rows |0.0016033700|

Source accuracy uses raw score≥.5 for real and score<.5 for fake.
It measures this discriminator on these two sources, not digit recognition, calibration
or sample realism. The gallery retains the first 40 fixed-bank outputs, without choosing
attractive samples. Most remain grey fields rather than convincing digits. A low D loss
or finite G loss does not turn this short game into a successful image model.

